[Music]  despite popular belief historians say  pies were not a feature of the pilgrims  first thanksgiving dinner  but in the years since they've become  the finishing touch at countless holiday  meals  this morning on the dish we head into  the kitchen with baker and food stylist  erin jean mcdowell  her first book 2017's the fearless baker  was one of the new york times best  baking books of the year  and her latest release the book on pie  is the number one best seller in its  category  on amazon  it's a pumpernickel pie crust with  sesame seeds avocados lemon juice and  some chili flakes to get a little spice  double crust chicken pot pie because the  crust is only on the top  that is my favorite apple pie these are  mixed berry hand pies  it is a tomato tart to tan which is an  upside  down puff pastry pie sweet or savory  aaron jean mcdowell lives and breathes  pie what is it about pie that separates  it from all of the desserts well i grew  up  eating a lot of pie so i think that  there's definitely like a big pie making  tradition  in the midwest pies are kind of a unique  thing with this very flaky crust  with a huge array of different fillings  and a huge array of different toppings  and that's why i love them is just  because i've been around them so much  pies were part of her childhood she grew  up making them in her grandmother's  kitchen  my name is erin jean is my middle name  and it's my grandma's name which is why  i use my full name and everything  because she's the one who taught me to  make pie oh  so i always use my full name as a little  homage to her who doesn't love  being in their grandmother's kitchen  it's one of my fondest memories and  that's absolutely one of the places  where i fell in love with baking  she's been perfecting her technique and  recipes ever since  but making a really good pie crust ain't  easy  that's also true and i just don't know  why it's so hard  well i think the number one ingredient  that people forget about  with pie crust is actually their hands  or whatever the tool is that they're  using  because the ingredients are simple in my  pie dough there are four ingredients  flour salt butter and water and ice  water  and ice water yes very good and cold  butter cold butter sometimes i even  put the bowl of flour in the freezer for  a little while before i start mixing  but it's really not so much about the  ingredients it's about the technique  [Music]  did you ever have the discussion with  your gran you know what i'm pretty good  at this  i need to go to high school the  inspiration for going to culinary school  actually came from some other members of  my family  i have three older brothers and two of  them are artists  and i desperately wanted to be an artist  but i  didn't seem to have any natural skill  with pencils or paints or  anything and then one day i came home  from an art class a ceramics class and  my mom was making a cake and she was  using a tool that i had used in the  ceramics studio  and it was like this huge light bulb  moment where i was like  what if food is my medium and so i  started right then and there i was about  15 years old and i started making a  whole bunch of really awful cakes  they were just terrible so mcdowell  decided to get some real-life training  after i got my first job in a bakery i  realized it is an art form  i could really do this the summer after  my senior year when most kids are like  you know  hanging with their friends all the time  i was going to bed at 7 00 pm  so that i could wake up in the middle of  the night and go to work but it was  there that i realized oh my gosh i  really  love this which gave her the confidence  to apply to the famed culinary institute  of america  the first time i went i went with my  parents to tour it  they said that the smile on my face it  was my first time being there and i was  just like  it was it was like meant to be i  couldn't imagine going anywhere else  from the first day i set foot on that  campus  a lot of recipes tell you how to do  something  but i like to know why i'm doing it  since graduation  the 33 year old has become a food  stylist i wrote the book on pie  author and a baking consultant on food  52.  a recipe and cookware site you have two  cookbooks under your belt  what's next i want to just keep teaching  so i love doing these videos i'm trying  to show the mistakes as well as showing  the success oh my god that is brilliant  i just want people to see you know  recipes say but don't over mix it but  what does over mixing look like  what is it because no one knows and then  they over mix it right  i believe the mistakes are what get us  to perfection 100  thanksgiving is my absolute favorite  holiday mainly because it's a great  excuse to make and eat a lot of pie  with so much to be thankful for even in  2020  she won't be able to be with her family  for the holidays  at least not in the traditional sense my  favorite thanksgiving tradition is  actually waking up early  when my mom is baking the rolls and we  eat some of the rolls fresh out of the  oven  slathered with butter before anyone else  has even come over and that's gathering  it with buttons yes  and it's sometimes just her and i or her  and my dad and i  and maybe my brother sharing this moment  before kind of all the craziness  happens and and it's a really special so  what will thanksgiving be like for you  this year well i'm gonna make those  rolls i'll tell you that that's one way  that i can be with them even without  being with them that's what's so amazing  about food  is that you know it's this  it's this incredible source of memory  it's this incredible source of  sustenance  it just gives so much  and look what we have oh my goodness  aaron g mcdowell i'm eating apple pie  and you know we're not going to be  together this thanksgiving so i thought  this was  oh this is so good we can all zoom  together we can zoom together  turkey zoom i'll bring you an apple